7. Demands that all parties take immediate steps to ensure the protection of civilians seeking humanitarian assistance, and stresses the need for accountability for all acts of violence against them;
8. Calls for the voluntary, safe and dignified return of all displaced Palestinians to their homes and neighbourhoods in all areas of Gaza, including the north, and stresses that any displacement must be consistent with international humanitarian law;
9. Calls upon all parties to refrain from unilateral actions, including incitement and violence against civilians, that undermine the two-State solution, and underscores the need for full respect for international law in the occupied Palestinian territory, including East Jerusalem;
10. Reaffirms that the Gaza Strip is an integral part of the Palestinian territory occupied in 1967 and stresses the importance of unifying the Gaza Strip with the West Bank under the Palestinian Authority;
11. Calls for the resumption of negotiations and diplomatic efforts under the auspices of Egypt, Qatar, the United States of America and other partners to reach a comprehensive ceasefire and a just, lasting and comprehensive peace, and urges all parties to engage in good faith;
12. Stresses the need for accountability for all violations of international humanitarian law and human rights law, and requests the Secretary-General to report to the Security Council within 30 days and thereafter every 60 days on the implementation of this resolution, including on humanitarian access, the protection of civilians, compliance with international law, and measures taken to ensure accountability for attacks on civilians, humanitarian personnel, medical personnel, journalists, diplomatic personnel and United Nations premises; calls upon all parties to cooperate with United Nations accountability mechanisms, including independent investigations into attacks on United Nations premises, humanitarian workers and civilians seeking humanitarian assistance; and calls upon all parties to comply with the provisional measures ordered by the International Court of Justice;
13. Decides to remain seized of the matter.

